    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4900A\n\nSPONSOR: ROLISON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Sergeant Elijah A. Briggs Memorial\nHighway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nDesignates a portion of the state highway system as the Sergeant Elijah\nA. Briggs Memorial Highway.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law by adding a new section 345-b to read\nas follows: Portion of the state highway system to be designated as the\n\"Sergeant Elijah A. Briggs Memorial Highway\". All that portion of state\nroute nine in the town of Fishkill, county of Dutchess, shall be desig-\nnated and known as the \"Sergeant Elija A. Briggs Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2: States that the commissioner of transportation shall provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signage of the state\nhighway system.\n\nSection 3: States the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Fishkill submitted resolution 2023-5 to request that a\nportion of the New York state route nine to be designated as the\n\"Sergeant Elija A. Briggs Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSergeant Briggs fought for the Union Army during the Civil War, during\nwhich he was wounded in service and was subsequently awarded the\nCongressional Medal of Honor for his bravery. Sergeant Briggs was honor-\nably discharged at the completion of the war and went on to raise a\nfamily within the boundaries of the Town of Fishkill.\n\nHe is buried in the Fishkill Rural Cemetery on Route 9 and the people of\nFishkill wish to honor his memory and bravery with this designation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
